---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Experience | Cabe Robertson"
    description="Professional experience of Cabe Robertson: engineering roles at ETV America (unmanned systems production, NASA SBIR), GILZ, Syndetix (RF jamming demonstrator), and the Mitchell Coding Group."
    ogTitle="Experience | Cabe Robertson"
    ogDescription="Internships and research in electrical, hardware, and test engineering."
    ogCard="experience"
>
<main id="main">
        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="section-head reveal in">
                    <span class="section-index">01</span>
                    <h1 class="section-title">Professional Experience</h1>
                </div>
                <p class="section-sub reveal in">Four engineering roles spanning defense RF hardware, unmanned systems production, embedded motor drive, and communications research.</p>

                <div class="log">
                    <!-- ETV America -->
                    <article class="log-entry reveal">
                        <span class="log-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
                        <div class="log-body">
                            <div class="log-head">
                                <h2>Electrical Engineering Intern &middot; Emerging Technology Ventures (ETV America)</h2>
                                <span class="log-date">Jul 2026 – Present</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tags">
                                <span class="tag">Unmanned Systems</span>
                                <span class="tag">AutoCAD</span>
                                <span class="tag">Procurement / BOM</span>
                                <span class="tag">Blue UAS / NDAA</span>
                                <span class="tag">NASA SBIR</span>
                            </div>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Solely responsible for standing up the company's unmanned systems production floor end to end: AutoCAD equipment layout, tooling and power specification, vendor qualification, and procurement, delivering a turnkey 7-person build area</li>
                                <li>Authored the capital-equipment budget and 59-line-item BOM (~$168K), sourcing every component to Blue UAS / NDAA-compliant vendors and delivering it as an audit-ready QuickBooks Enterprise import</li>
                                <li>Co-authored a 30-page NASA SBIR/STTR (CCRPP) proposal seeking a $2.5M matching award for an autonomous on-orbit inspection and repair system</li>
                                <li>Selected by company leadership to pitch at the NASA Moon to Mars Summit (Huntsville, AL, Sept 2026) on licensing NASA's VIPIR robotic inspection payload into company flight hardware, competing for a $10,000 award</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <!-- GILZ -->
                    <article class="log-entry reveal">
                        <span class="log-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
                        <div class="log-body">
                            <div class="log-head">
                                <h2>Electrical Engineering Intern &middot; <a href="https://www.gilz.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="company-link">GILZ LLC</a></h2>
                                <span class="log-date">Mar 2026 – May 2026</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tags">
                                <span class="tag">ESP32</span>
                                <span class="tag">BLDC Motors</span>
                                <span class="tag">PWM</span>
                                <span class="tag">Benchmarking</span>
                            </div>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Reverse-engineered a commercial BLDC blower to characterize motor voltage/current ratings and PWM response, defining the electrical drive specification</li>
                                <li>Programmed an ESP32 PWM controller (C / Arduino) adding 3 user-selectable speeds to a unit that shipped with no speed control</li>
                                <li>Ran a benchtop design of experiments sweeping duct and filter configurations against airflow, acoustic noise, temperature, and air velocity, identifying the configuration that cut noise ~10&nbsp;dB and raised airflow 20% versus stock</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <!-- Mitchell Coding Group -->
                    <article class="log-entry reveal">
                        <span class="log-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
                        <div class="log-body">
                            <div class="log-head">
                                <h2>Research Assistant &middot; <a href="https://www.mitchellcoding.com/Group.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="company-link">Mitchell Coding Group</a></h2>
                                <span class="log-date">Aug 2025 – Feb 2026</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tags">
                                <span class="tag">Python</span>
                                <span class="tag">MATLAB</span>
                                <span class="tag">Linear Algebra</span>
                                <span class="tag">Channel Coding</span>
                            </div>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Developed Python simulations of linear-algebra channel decoding, validating bit-error-rate performance across multiple encoding schemes under noise</li>
                                <li>Automated multi-hour experiment runs over contrasting input bit-strings to verify decoder reliability, processing statistics and generating publication-quality figures in MATLAB</li>
                                <li>Worked independently on an assigned research question over seven months, reporting results directly to the principal investigator</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="log-media">
                                <img src="plot1.jpg" alt="MATLAB plot of channel decoding simulation results" loading="lazy" width="1012" height="643">
                                <img src="plot2.jpg" alt="MATLAB plot visualizing experimental results" loading="lazy" width="973" height="632">
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <!-- Syndetix -->
                    <article class="log-entry reveal">
                        <span class="log-index" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
                        <div class="log-body">
                            <div class="log-head">
                                <h2>Hardware Engineering Intern &middot; <a href="https://www.syndetix.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="company-link">Syndetix Incorporated</a></h2>
                                <span class="log-date">Apr 2025 – Aug 2025</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tags">
                                <span class="tag">RF Systems</span>
                                <span class="tag">Hardware Prototyping</span>
                                <span class="tag">Technical Writing</span>
                                <span class="tag">Defense</span>
                            </div>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Designed and built a portable $219 field demonstration kit for an RF communication-jamming system shown to law enforcement and defense clients, ~56% cheaper than the $500 setup it replaced</li>
                                <li>Caught a wind tip-over failure during outdoor testing and engineered a lightweight stabilizing fix that kept the RF payload operational in high wind, without adding the ballast that would have cost portability</li>
                                <li>Resolved a 4-year-old server permission/synchronization bug, restoring reliable shared-file access company-wide</li>
                                <li>Authored the product user manual, standardizing setup, operation, and RF handling procedures for mission and training use</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Leadership -->
        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="section-head reveal">
                    <span class="section-index">02</span>
                    <h2 class="section-title">Leadership &amp; Involvement</h2>
                </div>
                <p class="section-sub reveal">Beyond internships, I lead initiatives that connect students with industry and grow our engineering community.</p>

                <div class="log">
                    <article class="log-entry reveal">
                        <span class="log-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
                        <div class="log-body">
                            <div class="log-head">
                                <h2>Vice President &middot; IEEE NMSU Student Chapter</h2>
                                <span class="log-date">Oct 2024 – Present</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tags tags--accent">
                                <span class="tag">External Affairs</span>
                                <span class="tag">Fundraising</span>
                                <span class="tag">Industry Relations</span>
                                <span class="tag">Mentorship</span>
                            </div>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Lead a $50,000 fundraising initiative to revitalize the chapter and the entire Electrical &amp; Computer Engineering department</li>
                                <li>Built the <a href="/ieee-bricks.html">Legacy Brick Project</a> behind it: alumni giving at the $500 level are recognized with an engraved commemorative brick, and chapter members produce each one themselves, from engraving file to machine shop, earning points toward the Rising Stars Conference delegation</li>
                                <li>Led the chapter turnaround that won NMSU's Most Improved Student Organization Award at the 2026 E-Council Banquet</li>
                                <li>Tripled active membership from 10 to 30+, and mentor members through hands-on soldering and troubleshooting workshops</li>
                                <li>Serve as primary liaison to industry sponsors, national IEEE, and campus organizations to secure collaborations and sponsorship</li>
                                <li>Hosted a pre-career-fair resume workshop, represented the chapter at the IEEE Rising Stars Conference 2026, and demonstrated a Brain–Computer Interface kit at the El Paso Science Festival 2026</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>
